sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Test as Concurrency test
  participant Blocker as Blocker transaction
  participant Publish as Publish contender, expected version 1
  participant Remove as Remove-last-step contender, expected version 1
  participant PG as PostgreSQL Course aggregate

  Test->>Blocker: BEGIN
  Blocker->>PG: SELECT Course FOR UPDATE
  PG-->>Blocker: Root row lock held

  par Publish request
    Publish->>PG: BEGIN and SELECT Course FOR UPDATE
  and Replace steps with empty list
    Remove->>PG: BEGIN and SELECT Course FOR UPDATE
  end
  Note over Publish,Remove: Both writers wait on the same Course root row
  Test->>PG: Observe two Lock waiters in pg_stat_activity
  Test->>Blocker: COMMIT
  Blocker->>PG: Release root lock

  Note over Publish,Remove: PostgreSQL chooses the first contender nondeterministically
  Publish->>PG: First contender reads version 1 and aggregate invariants
  Publish->>PG: Apply one valid mutation, set version 2, COMMIT
  PG-->>Remove: Grant the root lock after the first commit
  Remove->>PG: Read version 2
  Remove->>Remove: expected version 1 no longer matches
  Remove->>PG: ROLLBACK without a second mutation

  Test->>PG: Read final aggregate
  PG-->>Test: Exactly one version increment and one valid state
  Note over Test,PG: The winner can be either operation<br/>Archive versus feedback uses the same root lock pattern
